==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is a [[Catclaw Castle (Enemy Base)|Catclaw Castle]].
*2 [[Zoge]]s spawn after 8 seconds<sup>240f</sup>, delay 40~43.33 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Kroxo]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*1 [[Zory]] spawns after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Lord Gravey]] spawns as the boss.
**2 [[Zang Roo]]s spawn, delay 60~63.33 seconds<sup>1,800f~1,900f</sup>.
**3 [[Zory|Zories]] spawn, delay 46.67~50 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,500f</sup>.
**1 [[I.M. Phace]] spawns after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
It is highly recommended to get at least the ItF 2 treasures, as the I.M Phace and Kroxos will prove difficult otherwise. The zombies also make this hard to stall, so it is recommended to have [[Welterweight Cat (Rare Cat)|Heavyweight Cat]] to prevent them from burrowing. Thankfully, meatshielding works on both Gravey and I.M Phace at the same time, but the Zories can make this difficult with their tunneling, and getting a Heavyweight in time can prove cumbersome. Thankfully, there are only 3 of them and 2 of the Zang Roos, so it is unlikely for the bosses to get all the way to your base. Having a good anti-floater like [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Butterfly Cat]] or can help make this stage much easier.

==Hints==
These hints only appear as defeat messages given upon losing the stage.
*This stage is nearly impossible to beat<br>before collecting all Treasures from<br>Into the Future Ch. 2.
*Save enough Money to counter<br>Zombies that burrow into the ground<br>to pop up near your Cat Base.

